{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall stand on the rock.</b> It is the top of the mountain, for so it is written, ונצבת לי שם על ראש ההר (below 34:2), and He said that he shall stand there, and on account of the Glory He Himself will place him in the cleft of the rock, for so it is written ושמתיך — not that he himself shall enter. Now I shall mention the general sense of the pericope. The Gaon [Saadia] said that HaShem said to Moses: Bring this people up from this place where they sinned, and in another place I will pardon them. And Moses replied: If You do not turn back Your anger now in this place, do not bring us up from here. But what seems correct to me is that since HaShem said to him ושלחתי לפניך מלאך (v. 2), then Moses replied: ואתה לא הודעתני את אשר תשלח עמי (v. 12) — whether it is the one of whom it is written כי שמי בקרבו (above 23:21). And HaShem answered him: אני בעצמי אלך והנחותי לך (v. 14). And behold, the sense of לך is: with you alone I will go, and I will not dwell among the children of Israel. Therefore Moses replied: אם אין פניך הולכים עם הגוי הזה — that nation which He mentioned above; and see that עמך הגוי הזה (v. 13) is not in the plural. And a faithful witness to this interpretation: ובמה יודע איפה כי מצאתי חן בעיניך אני ועמך הלא בלכתך עמנו (v. 16). And HaShem answered: גם את הדבר הזה אשר דברת אעשה כי מצאת חן בעיני (v. 17). And because of this Moses rejoiced and said ילך נא ד׳ בקרבנו (below 34:9) — the opposite of כי לא אעלה בקרבך (v. 3). And Moses asked to see HaShem, and HaShem answered him: כי לא יראני האדם וחי (v. 20). And this is the truth, for the perceiving faculties do not perceive [Him], only the accidents. Therefore ויראו את אלהי ישראל (above 24:10), also ואראה את ד׳ (Isaiah 6:1), and likewise the prophecy of Ezekiel — all במראות אלהים. And behold, He said here וראית את אחורי (v. 23), and in another place ותמונת ד׳ יביט (Numbers 12:8). And these matters require lengthy explanation. The Gaon [Saadia] said that the face is the face of the light, and the analogy is the face of the sun, and the back is what remains of the light attached to a thing — and there is no need for all this. But before I explain this, I say: know that HaShem did not speak with Moses פנים אל פנים except on the third forty days and onward, and on account of HaShem being על פניו then, קרן עור פניו — for the beginning of his prophecy was by means of the angel seen in the bush, and there it is written ויאמר ד׳ (above 3:7), and likewise וד׳ הולך לפניהם יומם (above 13:21), for the emissary speaks in the tongue of the sender. And this day on which Moses saw what he asked was for him like the day of the giving of the Torah to Israel, and no person reached before him or after him to his level. And our sages said that He showed him the knot of tefillin, and their words are correct — only not as the sages of our generation explain it, that it is as it sounds, for it is a deep sod." "<b>Says Abraham the author.</b> I have already explained the written Name that is not read — it is the Name of the essence, and the essence is the Glory. And when you sum the numerical value of all its letters it comes to seventy-two; therefore our sages said that it is the explicit Name. And when you combine the first square with the middle square, it will in truth equal the numerical value of the Name. Likewise the combinations of the five wandering stars — also when you combine the letters that a person pronounces in half of the Name, it will equal the numerical value of the Name. And when you combine the squares of the pairs that are in the first rank, they will equal the combined value of half the Name. And when you double the first half of the Name over the [other] half, you will find the squares of the odd-positioned ones. And when you subtract the first square from the second square, there will remain the cube of the second letter. And if you subtract the second square from the third square, there will remain in sum the cube of the third letter. And this honored Name is the One that stands by itself, and has no need for another before it. And if you consider it from the perspective of number, it is the head of all, and all number [comes] from the units — it is the One that is all; therefore the sod of prayers and praises, and the sense of והתגדלתי והתקדשתי (Ezekiel 38:23), and also אשר בך אתפאר (Isaiah 49:3). And behold, the One has no form, and it is as a generality for all forms, for from it they emerged. And behold, the supernal natures — they are the luminaries and the stars — have no face and back, nor does the supernal soul of man, nor do the ministering angels of above, nor the Supreme of supremes. And behold, the line between two points: the point near the active cause is שר הפנים and שר הכח, and the other point is the end of the power. And the movement of man is forward, and the supernal body to the right, and the vegetative upward. And behold, Moses, peace be upon him, could know and see with the eye of his heart how the creatures cleave to the Creator, called אחורים — and by way of the Glory there is no power in a creature to know this, and this is כי לא יראני האדם וחי, because the soul of man is with the body. And behold, after the death of the understanding one, his soul reaches a high level that it does not attain in the life of man. And behold, Moses returned [to the] general, therefore HaShem said ידעתיך בשם, for He alone knows the particulars and their parts by way of the general. Because the most honored in the earth is man, therefore the form of the cherubim; and the most honored among man is Israel, therefore the matter of the knot of tefillin; and therefore it is written in שיעור קומה. For HaShem is the creator of every body, and everything honored of body and despised of body is accident. And Rabbi Ishmael said: Whoever knows the measure of his Creator is assured that he is a son of the world to come — and I and Rabbi Akiva are guarantors in this matter. And this is נעשה אדם בצלמנו כדמותנו (Genesis 1:26). And know that all the plants and living creatures in the earth, and the fowl and the beast and the wild animal and the creeping thing and every man — are tied to forty-eight forms of the sphere, and this is אשר חלק ד׳ אלהיך אותם לכל העמים (Deuteronomy 4:19). And those who illumine their eyes further from this matter — perhaps they knew this and did not wish to reveal the sod to students, and a faithful witness: ולא חלק להם (Deuteronomy 29:25). And it is known that the combinations are one hundred and twenty — the combinations of seven. And the largest combination among all of them in number is one, and the second combination is one and twenty, and corresponding to them the combination of five — likewise. And this number comes from seven, and the combination of three is five and thirty, which also comes from seven combinations; and likewise the combination of four. And behold, the combination of six is seven, and the combinations that encompass the families for all the earth according to the lot of each border of the seven borders that are all the inhabited world — and concerning them it is written: אתה הצבת כל גבולות ארץ קיץ וחורף (Psalms 74:17), which changes in all the borders: אתה יצרתם. And the change does not come from the sun, only because of its inclination toward the north and south side. And behold, the two upper combinations in the sign of Aries return to the sign of their conjunction to the ninth sign every nine hundred and sixty years, and both revolve from the sign of their conjunction to the ninth sign every twenty years; thus they revolve twelve times until two hundred and forty years, and from there they revolve by this number and in this manner, in the earthy signs, also in the airy signs, also in the watery signs. And let it not enter your heart that the four elements are in the heavens, and that there is heat in the sun and cold in the moon and in Saturn — far be it, far be it — for the supernal creatures are honored, and concerning them it is written: כי הוא צוה ונבראו, ויעמידם לעד לעולם חוק נתן ולא יעבור (Psalms 148:5–6). Rather they were created thus for the sake of the receivers. And behold, the ministers cannot change their way, and that one of them pass the decree that HaShem gave it; also all the host of heaven and the lower ones receive from them according to their alignment. Therefore לא ייטיבו ולא ירעו. And behold, one who worships the work of the heavens — they will not benefit him except what is decreed upon him according to the arrangement of his natal stars, thus will befall him — unless the supernal power guards him more than the power of the stars, that he cleave to it; then he will escape the decrees. And I shall give you a weighty parable: that the arrangement of the stars was such that a river would swell over a certain city and sweep away people or they would die. And a prophet came and warned them to turn back to HaShem before the day of their evil came, and they turned back to Him with all their heart. And because they cleaved to Him, He put it in their hearts that the people of the city would go outside to pray to HaShem, and behold, they did so. And on that day the river suddenly swelled as is its way, as we have seen with our own eyes many times, and it swept away the whole city. And behold, the decree of HaShem did not turn away, yet it saved them. And consider that the ministers run like horses running on a track, and they do not run to do evil or to do good — rather, thus is their way. And consider that on the track a blind man does not know the habits of the horses, when they go right or left, and he leans on a sighted man who knows their course — and behold, he guards him, for when they run to this side he leads the blind man to the other side, and the running of the horse does not change and the blind man is saved. And because of this HaShem said: after אשר חלק (Deuteronomy 4:19) — ואתכם לקח ד׳ להיות לו לעם נחלה (ibid. v. 20). Thus לא כאלה חלק יעקב כי יוצר הכל הוא (Jeremiah 51:19). And this is ונפלינו אני ועמך (above v. 16). And this is what the sages of blessed memory said: אין מזל לישראל — as long as they keep the Torah. And if they do not keep it, the mazzal will rule over them, as is experienced. For every combination and every Aquarius in a bad arrangement — behold, evil will come to Israel, and those who know the wisdom of the mazzalot will acknowledge this. And behold, the arrangement of the heavens was in a combination that they would remain in the exile of Egypt many more years, and because they cried out to HaShem and turned back to Him, HaShem saved them. And as it happens to the collective, so it happens to the individual; therefore שומר תורה אשרהו (Proverbs 29:18)." "And behold, ידעתיך בשם (above v. 12) — like יודע ד׳ דרך צדיקים (Psalms 1:6)." "And behold, הראני נא (above v. 18) is not in a vision of the eye." "And behold, על פניך (v. 19) — על פניך the inner ones, and they are the face of the heart." "And the sense of כל טובי (ibid.) — that it is not like 'the all,' and not in all, and not with all." "And the sense of וחנותי את אשר אחון — concerning Moses: for I will cause all my goodness to pass before your face, and before my passing I will have compassion on you, and this is אסוך כפי עליך. And behold, this is the interpretation: והכף כדמות סתר — like one concealing the essence of the sun with his palm, so that his soul does not separate from his body." "And behold, וראית את אחורי — from the aspect that He is the all, and His glory fills the all, and from Him is the all, and all their form is all. And this is ותמונת ד׳ יביט (Numbers 12:8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "The comment is dense with numerological and astrological material; many phrases are elliptical. כלי מרכבה allusion at 'שיעור קומה' rendered literally without expansion. The closing citation of Proverbs 29:18 uses only the second stich of the verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T20:28:39.208503326Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}